  "id": "recognition-threshold",
  "term": "recognition threshold",
  "definition": "In this packet, recognition threshold refers to the signal-to-noise ratio at which a person's speech recognition falls to 50% of their recognition score in quiet. It is used as an index of how well speech can be recognized in noise.",
